			<div class="content" id="post-content-4810859">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> Tale</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> On the fence, likely either Horror/Comedy or Horror/Action</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong></p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A Dr. Wondertainment product vs The Yule-Man</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The Yule Man has picked a household that might be able to put up more of a fight against him than he bargained for.</p>
<p>The family's introduction takes precedence over the Yule Man, who remains more of a background figure initially glimpsed mostly by the youngest child. In this time family relationships are established and some unease is presented re: someone watching them</p>
<p>As the Weissnacht escalates, what was initially seen as one child's active imagination, is being called into question, but more mundane explanations are given. Still, better safe than sorry, so in this phase the kids are allowed to 'open one present early' and given their Wondertainment Custom Pets to let hatch wherever they want and see what they become!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Paranoia increases as the Event enters its second phase where the Yule Man is apparently inside the house on and off, but nobody can find anything. At this point, the older sibling is genuinely concerned and sets out to hatch his pet into something he can train as a 'guard dog'.</p>
<p>The climax, naturally, is when the Yule Man attacks. This, I hope, will be an exciting fight for their lives against him.</p>
<p>At this phase, the time comes for the family to fight back with&#8230; well, everything at hand. Possibly a tense 'hide and seek' style event of running/attacking the Yule Man, and a narrow 'victory' albeit with collateral damage, injuries and very likely a death or two.</p>
<p>Possibly a stinger involving a letter from Dr. Wondertainment. Possibly a sort of congratulations for proving the superiority of his products over those of 'his competitor'.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Christmas in the Foundation-Verse is sometimes a very terrifying ordeal.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> At the moment, I'm almost imagining something like Gremlins vs Krampus with a combination of the pets guarding their humans and the use of Wondertainment Products in traps/tricks/etc.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
