			<div class="content" id="post-content-4810909">
									

<p>I'm very interested in this for some reason, and I wanna see how it turns out.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Here,&nbsp;have&nbsp;some&nbsp;considerations</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[-]&nbsp;OK,&nbsp;now&nbsp;give&nbsp;me&nbsp;back&nbsp;my&nbsp;considerations</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>So, this obviously isn't a concept, it's still an <em>idea</em>, so I can't give you any exact critique. Therefore, I'll just give you some things to consider while developing it:</p>
<p>First, you can create any Wondertainment product you want, you don't <em>need</em> to use the ones that are already established. And I personally won't recommend to use any of the Little Misters, as this tale is already holding on a &quot;famous&quot; character of the Foundation Universe.</p>
<p>Following that, a &quot;custom pet&quot;, as in &quot;a genetically altered animal created by Wondertainment in order to care for its owner&quot;, can be your best option here. It could be that the kid's parents have contacts within the anomalous cummunity and that's how the family got it? Adding on that, the kid could have more anomalous Wondertainment toys at hand.</p>
<p>Remember, they're going to fight for their life. <em>They don't need to read the warnings.</em></p>
<p>Of course, you will need to create an interesting story with character development and stuff. If done correctly, this table could be <em>great</em>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Overall, I like this. It still needs development, of course, but I think it <em>can</em> be great.</p>
<p>Feel free to contact the <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/butterfly-squad-roster">Butterfly Squad</a> to get more crit, or PM me to take another look!</p>
<hr />
<p>I've been summoned back by a PM. So let's do this!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Here,&nbsp;have&nbsp;some&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[-]&nbsp;OK,&nbsp;now&nbsp;give&nbsp;me&nbsp;back&nbsp;my&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>The family would be introduced quickly.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Be careful with this. Too quickly and the reader won't care for them. Maybe including only two kids (with one being older) would be better so you can deepen into their relationship? Maybe the family already had relationship problems before the Weissnacht Event? Or maybe they finally faced their relationship problems during the Weissnacht Event?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Possibly the parents initially think it might be either some group like the Foundation/UIU</p>
</blockquote>
<p>If the parents thought the Foundation/UIU/GOC found them, I don't think they would be living in that house anymore. They should be already running for their lives. Maybe they think it's just a friend of them? Maybe they think it's just a neighbor? &quot;Rural area&quot; doesn't necessarily means that there aren't moore people. Maybe they could have a discussion over this in which one wants to run while the other doesn't?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>possibly have them hatching their own pet now, in a more 'dangerous' environment to get something &quot;like a guard dog&quot;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Are they eggs? What I get with this is that the pet becomes something according to the enviroment it's hatched on&#8230;? Maybe the pet could be pre-dertermined and the parents just got they some &quot;normal&quot; dog/cat because the &quot;cooler&quot; ones were very expensive? Of course, these animals will still have anomalous properties. And maybe you could write some scene in which the teen sibling wants to train the pet to be &quot;like a guard dog&quot;?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This, I hope, will be an exciting fight for their lives against him.</p>
</blockquote>
<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">I hope too.</span> I don't think everything on this scene <em>needs</em> to be action. You want the tale to be <strong>Horror</strong>, don't ya? Maybe the kids hide somewhere? Maybe it could be like a Hide and Seek game with some sparks of action whenever the Yule Man finds someone?</p>
<p>Also, keep in mind this little sentence from SCP-4666:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The method of killing varies with the event, and will typically be preceded by some form of torture, which appears to serve a <strong>ritualistic purpose</strong>.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The &quot;ritual&quot; is never explained in the article itself, so maybe you can play with that. What does the Yule Man <em>wants</em>?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>albeit with some collateral damage and probably injuries…</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Remember: There's no such thing as a happiest ending. There could be sad, good, bad, even &quot;happy&quot; endings. But there's no &quot;happiest ending&quot;. A battle with an anomaly that has at least 500 years of experience is going to leave scars.</p>
<p>(What I want to say with the above is that you should kill someone. Maybe one of the pets or something.)</p>
<blockquote>
<p>[&#8230;] a letter from Dr. Wondertainment. Possibly a sort of congratulations for proving the superiority of his products over those of 'his competitor'.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The &quot;final punch&quot; needs to be done with a Wondertainment product if you want this to happen. Maybe a Wondertanment product would &quot;knock out&quot; the Yule Man for a few moments, and then the Sun rises, so it's ambiguous if the product defeated him or he just was out of time?</p>
<p>And I think this is the <em>best</em> ending you could have.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I'm seeing something like a 'Gremlins meets Home Alone'</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I was thinking more of <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Krampus_(film)">Krampus</a>. I personally think that the &quot;Home Alone&quot; thing would imply too much comedy, and SCP-4666 is one of the scariest articles on the wiki, so I don't think they would be compatible. I mean, if you figure out how to make it work, then do it.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Maybe even a &quot;Gamers Against Weed&quot; reference for the teenage sibling, but that might be reference overload.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I also think this would be a reference overload. Try to keep this between the Yule Man and Dr. Wondertainment.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Overall, I still like this, and I really hope you manage to post it by Christmas.</p>
<p>Feel free to contact a member of the <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/butterfly-squad-roster">Butterfly Squad</a> or go to #thecritters on the <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/chat-guide">IRC Chat</a> to get more crit, or PM me to take another look!</p>
<p>(I highly recommend reaching out to other people, as I can't hand out greenlights yet.)</p>

							</div>

								
