<p>Alrighty&#8230; since, I'm having trouble figuring out quoting for&#8230; some reason, I'll try and address your points numeral fashion and see what comes about.</p>
<p>1. I may have used &quot;quickly&quot; a bit too casually there, when I mostly meant to try and get the family as a whole introduced to the readers as early on in the story as I can manage. Certainly wouldn't do to have someone show up halfway in, after all!<br />
I do think you have a good point about keeping the cast on the smaller side and doing an older and younger sibling instead of three children in total, though, and most likely when I get to drafting that will be reflected.<br />
Some inter-family drama, also sounds like a good suggestion, particularly as it does fit with the themes of BOTH the slasher/horror genres and the holiday movie in hindsight&#8230; plenty to play with there!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>2. Also good points, they probably wouldn't be nearly so casual if a government agency or&#8230; The Foundation were believed to be pursuing them. Although I could see a debate happening along the lines of &quot;this could just be nothing&quot; and &quot;we have roots here, we can't just up and run&quot; as a line of contention. Possibly tying in with the above point about some sort of family frictions that could be addressed during the event itself.</p>
<p>3. I'd done a quick re-read of the Custom Pets and they do appear to be hatched and then heavily influenced by their environment for the form they take. Although, the idea of going for a cheaper model, maybe a Wondertainment take on those 'robot dogs' that were popular a while back could be more interesting. (I recall they'd had a great many animals done up in that fashion, including a T-Rex&#8230; I could see Dr. Wondertainment having a LOT of fun producing a small robot T-Rex for sale)</p>
<p>4. You make a good point about playing up the dread the Yule Man brings about with him, I may have been veering closer towards turning him into a slasher villain which&#8230; while his brutality certainly fits it, you are right, I think, about him being best used as not just an implacable monster, but something genuinely terrifying and not quite understood by anybody involved.<br />
I like the idea of using the house and property to try and hide from him, maybe let the family come to some wrong conclusions about how to stop him&#8230;</p>
<p>5. Regarding the 'happiest ending', you make another pretty good point. Although, depending on how early in his collecting he hits this family, just the fact that multiple small children are recovered from the sack he brought with him could automatically make it a pretty happy ending regardless&#8230; excepting potential pet deaths and the background knowledge that the Yule Man brutally murdered the families of each of those children and made them watch&#8230;</p>
<p>6. Going back to the above combined with the &quot;Wondertainment Product knockout/ambiguity&quot; that's a pretty spiffy idea and is quite likely now to work its way into the final product. Thanks!</p>
<p>7. Yeah, in hindsight the &quot;Home Alone&quot; element was more a call out to using things that aren't necessarily meant to be weapons to fend off a home invasion, but it would be hard to fit that much direct slapstick into things. Even the &quot;Gremlins&quot; moment was mostly me thinking of the Wondertainment Pets having a scene similar to when Gizmo finally started fighting back against the other Mogwai.</p>
<p>Thanks for the crits, I'll give myself a bit of time to think it over more thoroughly tonight and see if anyone else's attention is caught by late tomorrow. If not, might be time for a PM or at least a visit to the Critters like you said.<br />
I'll try and keep you in the loop as well since you seem interested! Besides, more thoughts can't hurt, eh?</p>
</div>
</div>
